2. docs/LINUX.md section 6 as reviewed: packages through QEMU --net -> FAILS
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Release-only layout: sigil-linux's cache ~/.cache/sigil-linux/
sigil-linux-f2-2026-10-22/ (fw_jump.bin, Image, sigil-f2.dtb, .ext4.zst,
SHA256SUMS), sigil-qemu.dtb fetched with the doc's curl -fLo from a file://
copy of the release asset (sha256 matches SHA256SUMS), disk unpacked with
zstd -d --sparse as sigil-linux does, then
  SIGIL_LINUX_DIR=$D bash ~/sigil/scripts/qemu_sigil_boot.sh --disk ~/sigil-disk.ext4 --net
Boots to "sigil login:" in 13.3 s. After `sudo sigil-qemu-net`, apt update
never completes:
  virtio_net virtio0 eth0: NETDEV WATCHDOG: CPU: 0: transmit queue 0 timed out 5760 ms
  /proc/interrupts:  13:  0  SiFive PLIC  8 Edge  virtio0     (no interrupt, ever)
  ip -s link eth0:   RX 0 bytes 0 packets; TX 0 bytes 0 packets 7 errors
Cause: QEMU 8.2.2 hw/riscv/virt.c (lines 1450-1462) wires virtio-mmio
interrupts to the PLIC of socket 1 when the machine has two or more sockets
("Try to use different IRQCHIP instance based device type"). Each NUMA node
of qemu_sigil_boot.sh is a socket; socket 1's only hart is not in the DT and
OpenSBI parks it, so hart 0 never sees a virtio interrupt. Not fixable in the
DT without running Linux on that hart; the docs now use a chroot instead
(below), and section 3 / section 8 say that --net passes no traffic.

3. docs/LINUX.md section 6 as fixed: chroot through qemu-user-static -> PASS
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
The fenced block of the "More packages" bullet, extracted from LINUX.md at
54137c8 and run as is with <packages> = sl and M = a private mount point:
  sudo apt-get install -y qemu-user-static
  M=/home/ubuntu/rel73-pkgtest/mnt; sudo mkdir -p $M
  sudo mount -o loop ~/sigil-disk.ext4 $M
  sudo mount --bind /dev $M/dev; sudo mount -t devpts devpts $M/dev/pts; sudo mount -t proc proc $M/proc
  sudo cp -L /etc/resolv.conf $M/etc/resolv.conf
  sudo chroot $M apt-get update
  sudo chroot $M apt-get install -y sl
  sudo umount $M/proc $M/dev/pts $M/dev $M
apt update: Fetched 16.5 MB in 5s; install: libncurses6 6.5+20250216-2 and
sl 5.02-1+b1, postinst and triggers (man-db, libc-bin) ran under qemu-user.
Whole block 18 s. Nothing left mounted; the host's /dev/pts untouched.
disk before: 917 MiB allocated, 8 GiB file; after: 1110 MiB allocated, 8 GiB.
e2fsck -fn: clean (26721/524288 files, 335365/2097152 blocks).
sigil-linux's ext4_bytes on the result: 8589934592 = file size (accepted).

